# Shell: Windows PowerShell only

This workspace runs on **Windows PowerShell** (`powershell`, v5.1). Bash syntax
fails. Generate every shell command in PowerShell-compatible form.

## Command chaining — NO `&&` or `||`

Windows PowerShell 5.1 does not support `&&` / `||`. The token `&&` errors with
`'&&' is not a valid statement separator in this version.`

- Run commands as **separate tool calls** (preferred — clearer output per step).
- Or chain with `;` when you don't care about failure between steps.
- For "run B only if A succeeds", use an explicit check:

```powershell
# ❌ BAD — bash only, errors in PowerShell
ls -la && echo "done" && ls apps 2>/dev/null

# ✅ GOOD — separate statements
Get-ChildItem
Write-Output "done"
Get-ChildItem apps -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

# ✅ GOOD — stop-on-error chain
if ($?) { npm run build } ; if ($?) { npm test }
```

## Other bash-isms to avoid

| Bash | PowerShell |
|------|-----------|
| `ls -la` | `Get-ChildItem` (`ls` is an alias but flags differ) |
| `cmd 2>/dev/null` | `cmd -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue` or `2>$null` |
| `export VAR=x` | `$env:VAR = "x"` |
| `rm -rf dir` | `Remove-Item dir -Recurse -Force` |
| `cat file` | use the Read tool (not `cat`) |
| `cmd1 \| grep x` | prefer the Grep tool; else `cmd1 \| Select-String x` |
| `$(cmd)` | `$(cmd)` works, but `&&`/`||` inside do not |

## Reminder

Prefer the dedicated tools (Read, Grep, Glob, StrReplace) over shell for file
operations. Reserve the shell for actual system/terminal commands, and keep
those commands PowerShell-native.
